%% state_06_flagged_review.mmd — FlaggedReview Status
%% Evidence status: Implemented.
%% Updated 2026-07-10 (verified).
%% Purpose: Flagged review lifecycle from detection to resolution
%% Scope: Anomaly detection → admin resolution
%% Excludes: Score recalculation detail (see act_03c)
%% Related: detect_anomaly_command.ts, resolve_flagged_review_command.ts

stateDiagram-v2
direction LR
    [*] --> pending : DetectAnomalyCommand<br/>finds anomaly pattern

    pending --> dismissed : Admin dismisses<br/>(false positive)
    pending --> confirmed : Admin confirms fraud<br/>(ResolveFlaggedReviewCommand)

    dismissed --> [*]
    confirmed --> [*]

    note right of pending
        SQL enum declares 6 flag_type values.
        detect_anomaly_command currently checks:
        ✅ bulk_same_level
        ✅ new_account_high
        ✅ mutual_high
        ⚠️ ip_collusion is documented as placeholder.
        ⚠️ No current check found for sudden_spike
           or frequency_anomaly.
        ──────────────────
        Flag rows are created when
        DetectAnomalyCommand finds
        a supported anomaly pattern.
        Current admin resolve flows go directly from
        pending -> dismissed/confirmed, even though
        SQL enum also allows 'reviewed'.
    end note

    note left of confirmed
        On confirmation (rollbackFraudulentReview):
        1. skill_review.is_fraud = true
        2. RecalculateRevieweeSkillScoresCommand
           (exclude fraud reviews)
        ──────────────────
        Only System Admin can resolve
        (superadmin / system_admin role)
    end note
